From 2487f27e16cacb969daa067c39ed9fd096ac642c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vkd3d-crossover <noreply@vkd3d-crossover.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:12:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 25/28] fix: pass shader interface types to SPIRV-Cross and fix
 vertex format classes

Problem: Pipeline creation rejected by Metal for interface mismatches D3D allows (one source of RE Engine E_OUTOFMEMORY/E_FAIL).

Root cause: Fragment output type != render target type (e.g. float4 -> R32_UINT), VS->PS interface type mismatches, and vertex attribute format class != shader input type (e.g. UInt4 -> float4) are legal in Vulkan/D3D12 but rejected by Metal.

Fix: Fill SPIRV-Cross fragment_output_basetypes from the color attachment formats and fragment_input_basetypes from the previous stage's outputs (single, unpacked outputs only), and serialize both in the pipeline cache. Reflect vertex shader input base types and remap the Metal vertex format to the shader's type class. Requires the SPIRV-Cross patches of this series (patches/spirv-cross).

Verified by: test_shader_io_mismatch 3 -> 0 failures; vkd3d-proton re-sweep 0 regressions.

Off switch: none
